Aurora includes code and behavior adapted from the following MIT-licensed
Horizon-family projects:

- Horizon / Horizon-TechNews: MIT, copyright (c) 2026 Thysrael.
  Aurora modules adapted from this project include the tech_news RSS/Hacker
  News source behavior and deterministic news scoring under
  src/aurora/modes/tech_news/.
- Horizon-Scholar: MIT, forked from Horizon and carrying the same MIT notice.
  Aurora modules adapted from this project include arXiv/OpenReview paper
  ingestion and deterministic scholar scoring under src/aurora/modes/scholar/.
- Horizon-Github / RepoRadar: MIT as declared in pyproject.toml and README.
  Aurora modules adapted from this project include GitHub search, README/tree
  fetch behavior, query preset validation, deterministic repository scoring,
  package-file extraction, and recently recommended suppression under
  src/aurora/modes/repo_learning/.

Aurora keeps these adaptations scoped to Aurora's SignalItem and shared pipeline
contracts. Generated outputs, historical reports, screenshots, and
secrets-bearing configs from the upstream projects are not copied into Aurora.
